From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Age of Decomp patch queue <aod-patches@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:19:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aod: answer other games' save data for the data-link bonuses

The game gives bonus rewards for other games' save data on the same
user: main.npdm grants it read access to three titles' saves, and its
own table (main+0x235a728, save kinds 6..8) holds 0100B2F01111C000,
Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity and Tears of the Kingdom. The runtime
answered IsSaveDataExisting and MountSaveDataReadOnly only for the
game's own id.

TOTK_LINKED_SAVES=1 (hwaoi.ini linked_saves, off by default, read when
the game asks) is the player saying they have those saves: the game is
told they exist, and MountSaveDataReadOnly mounts
<profile>/linked/<title id>/ read-only, empty unless the player put
that game's save there. Each title's first answer of each kind is
logged. Reported in iCosiSenpai/age-of-decomp#1 by Konia1234-Pega.
